  <data name="Settings_HideWhileGamingNote" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When a program Windows knows as a game is in front, even in a window, the island hides on that screen. Even with this off, nothing on the island moves while a game is in front, so it costs the game no frames.</value>
  </data>
