  </data>
  <data name="Settings_ClosedClear" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>See-through</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_ClosedLookNote" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Black, like the Mac's notch. Follow the theme takes the open island's colour and glass. See-through lets the taskbar or desktop behind show; it suits an island on the taskbar.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_IdleBar" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Thin bar when idle</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_IdleBarNote" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>With nothing going on the island shrinks to a thin bar, and opens when the pointer reaches it. Only the bar takes the pointer, so tabs and buttons around it stay clickable.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Performance" xml:space="preserve">
