  <data name="Settings_PerformanceGaming" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>While gaming</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_PerformanceAlways" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Always</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_PerformanceNote" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>FPS, CPU and GPU use and temperatures, memory and the time on the small island; pick what shows below. While on, the island stays over the game; with a game in front, pointing at it or clicking it doesn't open it. The GPU's temperature comes from its driver; the CPU's needs LibreHardwareMonitor or OpenHardwareMonitor running.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_YieldToFluentFlyout" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Make way for FluentFlyout</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_YieldToFluentFlyoutNote" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>FluentFlyout shows its own flyout on the volume and media keys too. While it runs, the island shows no volume HUD and no new-song banner, so the two don't overlap.</value>
  </data>
